---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site.config';

const { event, footer } = siteConfig;
const email = footer.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="19 September 2026"
  description="The terms for using the Axios '26 website and registration portal, and for taking part in the symposium at PSG College of Technology."
>
  <div class="lg-note">
    <b>In short:</b> register honestly, follow each event's rules and the
    campus code of conduct, and respect other participants. Coordinators'
    decisions on results are final. We may change the schedule if we have to,
    and we will tell you when we do.
  </div>

  <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the Axios '26 website at
    <a href="https://axios.psgtech.ac.in">axios.psgtech.ac.in</a> and
    <a href="https://axios.live">axios.live</a>, the registration portal at
    <a href="https://app-axios.psgtech.ac.in">app-axios.psgtech.ac.in</a>,
    and the Axios '26 symposium held on 25–26 September 2026 at
    {event.date.venueName}. Axios is organised by the
    {event.organizer.name}, {event.organizer.department},
    {event.organizer.collegeName} ("CSA", "we", "us").
  </p>
  <p>
    By registering or taking part, you agree to these terms and to our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not
    register.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who can take part</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Axios is open to students of recognised colleges and universities, and to invited alumni and guests.</li>
    <li>Bring a valid college ID card to the venue.</li>
    <li>If you are under 18, you need the consent of a parent or guardian to register.</li>
    <li>Each event sets its own team size and eligibility rules. Those rules apply in addition to these terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Your account and registration</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give accurate details when you register, and keep them up to date.</li>
    <li>Your account is for you alone. Do not share it or register on someone else's behalf without their permission.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for what happens under your account and for the team members you add.</li>
    <li>A registration is confirmed only when you receive a confirmation from the portal or by email. Spots in some events are limited and are filled in order.</li>
    <li>Your registration is personal and cannot be transferred or sold.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Fees, payments and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Where an event, pass or service carries a fee, the amount is shown before
    you pay. Payments are processed by Razorpay. Fees are not refundable,
    except where we cancel the event or item you paid for; in that case we
    refund you in full to the original payment method.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Accommodation</h2>
  <p>
    Limited hostel accommodation is offered on a first come, first served
    basis. Requesting it does not guarantee a place until it is confirmed.
    Guests must follow the hostel's rules and the instructions of the
    accommodation coordinators.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Code of conduct</h2>
  <p>At the venue and online, you agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>harass, threaten, discriminate against or bully anyone;</li>
    <li>cheat, plagiarise, share answers or use tools an event's rules forbid;</li>
    <li>attack, probe or disrupt the website, the portal, event systems or college networks, except inside a Capture-the-Flag event's stated scope;</li>
    <li>damage college property or bring prohibited items onto campus;</li>
    <li>be under the influence of alcohol or drugs at the event.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You must also follow the rules of PSG College of Technology while on
    campus. We may disqualify anyone who breaks these rules, withdraw their
    prizes and certificates, and ask them to leave the venue, without a
    refund.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Results, prizes and certificates</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Judges and event coordinators decide results. Their decisions are final.</li>
    <li>Prizes are awarded as announced for each event. Prizes may be shared or withheld if an event has too few entries, or if no entry meets the standard.</li>
    <li>Prize money may be paid by bank transfer after the event, and may require proof of identity and college enrolment.</li>
    <li>Participation certificates are issued to those who were checked in at the event.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Your submissions</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of the work you submit. You allow CSA to display, judge
    and showcase it for Axios and its promotion, with credit to you. You
    confirm that your submission is your own and does not infringe anyone
    else's rights.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Photos and recordings</h2>
  <p>
    Axios is photographed and filmed. By attending, you agree that you may
    appear in photos and videos that we publish to cover the event. To opt
    out, or to ask us to remove a photo of you, email
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to the event</h2>
  <p>
    We may change the schedule, venue, format, rules or prizes, or cancel an
    event, if circumstances require it. We will post changes on this website
    or email registered participants. We are not responsible for travel or
    other costs you incur because of a change.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Website content</h2>
  <p>
    The Axios name, logos, artwork and website content belong to CSA or to
    their owners, including sponsors whose logos appear with permission. Do
    not reuse them without our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Your safety and liability</h2>
  <p>
    You take part at your own risk and are responsible for your own belongings.
    To the extent the law allows, CSA and PSG College of Technology are not
    liable for loss, theft, injury or damage arising from your participation,
    except where caused by our negligence. The website and portal are provided
    "as is", and we do not promise that they will always be available or free
    of errors.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute is subject to
    the courts at Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version.
    If you keep using the site or portal after a change, you accept the
    updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <b>{event.organizer.name}</b><br />
    {event.organizer.department}<br />
    {event.organizer.collegeName}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
